{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Daughters, your honored ones</b> — from the root יקר, for your honored handmaidens who are with them are daughters of kings. And one who says it is from the root בקורת — he has not spoken rightly, for there is no dispute that it is written with a yod; rather, the dispute is between the masters of the tradition and the reading, for one reads ביקרותיך like בימינו, and the second like מישיני עפר." "<b>And the queen-consort</b> — she is the one prepared, destined for the couch, and the proof is the word ישגלנה. And according to the one who says that this psalm was said about David, it is in its literal sense, and about the Messiah — 'daughters of kings, the honored ones' and 'the queen-consort' are his state."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:56.018461040Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}